Poem:
page 1 ending
You asked me to write again after meeting you.
So here's what I did for u.

5 feet of quite magic met in person

When you said you wanted that curler,
for a second,
I thought about buying it for you.

But then my mind started asking silly questions...
 
How?
You’re far away.
What if you don’t like it?
What would you tell at home?

And somewhere between all those thoughts,
I realized something.

I didn’t just want to send you gifts.

I wanted to see you.

I’ve already heard your voice,
your laugh,
your sadness,
your bullying,
your laziness,
your nonstop blabbering...

But I wanted to witness all of it in person.

That’s why I came all the way from a long distance,
just to spend a few hours with you.

And honestly?

Even if it was only for two minutes...
I still would’ve come.



need to create like carycacher

----------------------------------------------------------------
 
then that day finally came 

i traveled from chennai to trichy 

just to see you!

I come to pick you up at bus stand,

and there you are , waiting for me in the middle of all that noisy afternoon traffic.

black dress,
headphones,
backpack, 
tiny earings, 
your bangleless hands.
Loose hair dancing in the hot midday wind.

I took you on my bike,
and we ended up going to a café
even though I never really planned any of it.

And somewhere in the middle of the road,
right in front of the café,
with absolutely no surprise planning or dramatic setup,
I just awkwardly pulled the gift from my bike and handed it to you.

When you started opening it,
a part of me wanted to record everything—
your reaction,
your smile,
your excitement.

But then I remembered something.

There’s a Latin phrase:
“Carpe Diem.”

Seize the moment.

So instead of watching you through a camera,
I wanted to stay inside that moment with you.

The way you opened the gift…

You didn’t tear the wrapping apart.
You unfolded it slowly,
layer by layer,

And the expressions on your face—
your excitement,
your happiness,
that quiet little joy—

somehow made the entire journey worth it.

